            {
                "entry_id": "3296226c-1636-3177-b86a-b7d999c83138",
                "word": "ALT",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7319615c-29e6-320b-876a-3fe57760806f",
                        "entry_id": "3296226c-1636-3177-b86a-b7d999c83138",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of alanine transaminase."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7d7bf70-5607-488a-841e-1b5f6b56df48",
                                "sense_id": "7319615c-29e6-320b-876a-3fe57760806f",
                                "text": "Furthermore, wedelolactone also increased the activities of superoxidase dismutase (SOD) and glutathione peroxidase (GSH-Px) and decreased the level of the lipid peroxidation product malondialdehyde (MDA) in the liver, therefore decreasing the activity of alanine aminotransferase (ALT)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "2479a5e0-c06a-305c-a326-201b7209bbbd",
                "word": "alt",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5b7dbb11-b1da-4998-8246-7eb9b255778d",
                        "entry_id": "2479a5e0-c06a-305c-a326-201b7209bbbd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "alts"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad",
                        "entry_id": "2479a5e0-c06a-305c-a326-201b7209bbbd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of altbier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d7206e6-d7a4-425f-ab2b-9a6caf315699",
                                "sense_id": "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad",
                                "text": "Top-fermenting ales are still brewed, notably the alts of Düsseldorf and kölsches of Cologne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "471f67cd-3407-4315-aceb-5cb6cd1f7acf",
                                "sense_id": "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad",
                                "text": "On average, the mash temperatures used in the NHC second-round alts and kölschs were higher, at 153 °F (67 °C) and 151 °F (66 °C) respectively."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2319ac94-48f8-46fe-a03a-6dc16dbcea7f",
                                "sense_id": "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad",
                                "text": "In the last two days I have drunk 10 different beers in each city and feel the Kölsches were within a narrower flavor profile, being relatively similar to each other, whereas Alts had more range of aroma and flavor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07c7ec82-7065-494a-871f-838d89f6004d",
                                "sense_id": "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad",
                                "text": "Ale yeasts are often described as top fermenting, but top cropping would probably be a better description: the yeast ferments at all levels throughout the liquid, but once its work is done it collects at the top of the fermenting vessel (traditionally these vessels would have been open at the top). Family members include bitters, porters, stouts, alts and kölschs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "c0432c2f-1b22-4083-b316-ef218f764e5a",
                        "source_entry_id": "2479a5e0-c06a-305c-a326-201b7209bbbd",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "880a4c43-9ea0-3e10-8c52-a0da6389f6ad"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
                        "word": "altbier"
                    }
                ]
            },
